From 7712431385d6b9a553a5ac610f86b1330542eecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 04:06:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add colorful icon chips throughout the Risk Story tab

Replaces flat/uniform icons with a small tone-tinted IconChip pattern
reused across all six sub-tabs: peril icons (fire/wind/flood/crime/GL)
on the scorecard and score-derivation accordion, per-card colors on
Risk Protections, colored COPE glyphs replacing the black letter
boxes, a leading colored icon per row in Data Sources, icon headers on
the Map & GIS stat cards, and subject icons on Satellite Imagery
observations. Colors are drawn from the existing brand palette
(electric/iris/leaf/coral/amber) and kept distinct from the
leaf/amber/coral severity coloring already used on scores and status
chips.
---
